          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How are lab grown diamonds made?",
            "answer": "<p>A <strong>lab grown diamond</strong> is formed by recreating the same natural conditions found deep within the earth, only with precision and cutting-edge technology. Using methods such as HPHT and CVD, carbon atoms come together in controlled environments to form a crystal identical to a mined diamond. Every stone carries the same structure, brilliance, and durability, but with a more thoughtful and innovative origin. It’s this modern craftsmanship that inspires so many to buy lab grown diamonds at Gemlux Jewels and embrace the future of fine jewelry.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_2": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How long have lab grown diamonds been around?",
            "answer": "<p>Lab grown diamonds have existed since the 1950s, originally developed for industrial use. Over time, technology evolved to produce gem-quality stones suitable for fine jewelry. Their recent rise in popularity, amplified by fashion icons and celebrities, has made them one of the most exciting trends in the industry.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_3": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Are lab grown diamonds ethical?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes, lab grown diamonds are considered an ethical choice because they’re created without mining and remain entirely conflict-free. Their low environmental impact makes them especially appealing to those who value thoughtful, responsible luxury. As more people embrace sustainability in their jewelry decisions, many are choosing to shop for lab grown diamonds when selecting pieces meant to last.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_4": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Do Lab Grown Diamonds or Moissanite come with a Certificate?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes, Diamondrensu's lab-grown diamonds are certified by IGI or GIA, ensuring their quality and authenticity. Additionally, our moissanite come with a Gemluxjewels certificate of authenticity, guaranteeing their premium quality. This certification provides assurance of ethical sourcing and top-notch craftsmanship for every gemstone purchased from us.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_5": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How Should I Care For My Jewellery?",
            "answer": "<p>Caring for your titanium jewellery is effortless. Simply wash it occasionally with warm water and a mild soap, then gently pat it dry with a soft cloth. Avoid using harsh chemicals or abrasive cleaners to keep it looking brand new.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_6": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can Titanium Jewellery Rust Or Corrode?",
            "answer": "<p>No, not at all. Titanium is uniquely highly resistant to rust and corrosion. You can expose it to water, sweat, and even salt water without worrying about it oxidizing, tarnishing, or turning your skin green.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_7": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is Titanium Jewellery Suitable For Daily Wear?",
            "answer": "<p>Absolutely. Because titanium is incredibly lightweight and hypoallergenic, it is one of the most comfortable metals you can wear. It is designed specifically to be a piece you can put on and never have to take off.</p>"
          }
        },
